<article class="env-corollary" id="CB7B">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/CB7B">Corollary <span data-tag="CB7B">5.5.5.8</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a presentable $\infty $-category, let $S$ be a saturated collection of morphisms of $\calC $, and suppose that $S$ is of small generation. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { &  Y \ar [dr]^{g} &  \\ X \ar [ur]^{f} \ar [rr]^{h} &  &  Z}  \]
</div>
  <p> be a commutative diagram in $\calC $. If $f$ and $h$ belong to $S$, then $g$ belongs to $S$. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Combine Propositions <a href="/tag/B444" data-tag="B444">5.5.5.7</a>, <a href="/tag/94A7" data-tag="94A7">5.2.8.11</a>, and <a href="/tag/CBA5" data-tag="CBA5">5.2.8.6</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>